# Mana Battle game server — TLS reverse proxy for the Docker/Compose deployment.
#
# Terminates TLS (Let's Encrypt via Caddy automatic HTTPS) on 80/443 and
# reverse-proxies to the `server` compose service on :8787 (plain HTTP).
#
#   player ──https──▶ Cloudflare ──https──▶ Caddy (:80/:443) ──▶ server:8787
#
# Requirements:
#   - DNS: api.manabattle.com proxied by Cloudflare (orange cloud) → the VM.
#   - Cloudflare SSL/TLS mode: "Full (strict)" — CF re-encrypts to Caddy,
#     which serves a valid Let's Encrypt cert for the domain.
#   - Delete any Cloudflare origin rule that overrides the destination port —
#     CF must reach Caddy on 443, not the server's raw 8787.
#   - VCN security list: open 80 (ACME HTTP-01) and 443; the server's :8787
#     stays host-local (127.0.0.1 mapping in compose.yaml).
#
# The site address comes from MANA_API_DOMAIN (set in compose.yaml from the
# root .env; default api.manabattle.com). If the first Let's Encrypt issuance
# stalls behind Cloudflare, grey-cloud the DNS record for a minute so HTTP-01
# can reach :80 directly, then re-proxy.

{$MANA_API_DOMAIN:api.manabattle.com} {
	reverse_proxy server:8787
}
